-- coa26-ch1.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 42 (Statutory Auditors), Chapter 1 (Introductory),
-- ss 1209 to 1211, lines 16996-17028 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer). Every decision function here
-- answers MAYBE BOOLEAN.
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words ("means", "if", "only if", "where", a flat negative). Each such
--               branch carries a comment  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<quoted words>"
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide (silent, list not closed, includes, undefined term, points outside the
--               text, limited by its own wording). Each such branch carries  -- NOTHING-kind (<why>)
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. A borrowed answer (another Act, an order, another part's section)
--   is an INPUT of type MAYBE BOOLEAN, and NOTHING passes through as NOTHING.
--
-- Every top-level name begins with the label of the provision it implements.

§ `Part 42 -- Statutory Auditors`

§§ `Chapter 1 -- Introductory`

-- ---- s 1209: Main purposes of Part ---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 1209 states the purposes of the Part and creates no rule (coverage: inert, reason 1). Nothing is declared for it.

-- ---- s 1210: Meaning of "statutory auditor" etc -------------------------------------------------------

-- s 1210(1)(c)(i) and (ii) ask whether the friendly society is an "insurer" or an "issuer": see s 1210(3) below.
-- s 1210(1)(d) and (g) are blank in this text (coverage: repealed or blank).
-- src:17003 | (1) In this Part “statutory auditor” means—
-- src:17004 | (a) a person appointed as auditor under Part 16 of this Act,
-- src:17005 | (b) a person appointed as auditor under section 77 of or Schedule 11 to the Building Societies Act 1986 (c. 53),
-- src:17006 | (c) a person appointed as auditor of a friendly society under section 72 of or Schedule 14 to the Friendly Societies Act 1992, where that society is—
-- src:17007 | (i) an insurer, or
-- src:17008 | (ii) an issuer whose transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market;
-- src:17009 | (d) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:17010 | (e) a person appointed as auditor for the purposes of regulation 5 of the Insurance Accounts Directive (Lloyd's Syndicate and Aggregate Accounts) Regulations 2008 or appointed to report on the “aggregate accounts” within the meaning of those Regulations,
-- src:17011 | (f) a person appointed as auditor of an insurance undertaking for the purposes of the Insurance Accounts Directive (Miscellaneous Insurance Undertakings) Regulations 2008,
-- src:17012 | (g) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:17013 | (h) a person appointed as auditor of a prescribed person under a prescribed enactment authorising or requiring the appointment;
-- src:17014 | and the expressions “statutory audit” and “statutory audit work” are to be construed accordingly.
@ref s 1210(1) Meaning of "statutory auditor" (src:17003-17014)
GIVEN `appointed as auditor under Part 16 of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `appointed as auditor under section 77 of or Schedule 11 to the Building Societies Act 1986` IS A BOOLEAN
      `appointed as auditor of a friendly society under section 72 of or Schedule 14 to the Friendly Societies Act 1992` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that friendly society is an insurer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `that friendly society is an issuer whose transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `appointed as auditor for the purposes of regulation 5 of the Insurance Accounts Directive (Lloyd's Syndicate and Aggregate Accounts) Regulations 2008 or appointed to report on the aggregate accounts within the meaning of those Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `appointed as auditor of an insurance undertaking for the purposes of the Insurance Accounts Directive (Miscellaneous Insurance Undertakings) Regulations 2008` IS A BOOLEAN
      `appointed as auditor of a prescribed person under a prescribed enactment authorising or requiring the appointment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1210(1) the person is a statutory auditor` MEANS
    -- JUST TRUE when some limb holds; JUST FALSE only when every limb is JUST FALSE (the definition says "means");
    -- NOTHING when no limb holds but a borrowed answer is not known (NOTHING-kind (points outside the text)).
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Part “statutory auditor” means—"
    `coa26 support any of the answers` `the limbs of subsection (1)`
    WHERE
        `the limbs of subsection (1)` MEANS
            LIST JUST `appointed as auditor under Part 16 of this Act`                                              -- (a)
               , JUST `appointed as auditor under section 77 of or Schedule 11 to the Building Societies Act 1986`  -- (b)
               , `limb (c) friendly society auditor`                                                                -- (c)
               , JUST `appointed as auditor for the purposes of regulation 5 of the Insurance Accounts Directive (Lloyd's Syndicate and Aggregate Accounts) Regulations 2008 or appointed to report on the aggregate accounts within the meaning of those Regulations`  -- (e)
               , JUST `appointed as auditor of an insurance undertaking for the purposes of the Insurance Accounts Directive (Miscellaneous Insurance Undertakings) Regulations 2008`  -- (f)
               , `limb (h) prescribed person`                                                                       -- (h)
        `limb (c) friendly society auditor` MEANS
            IF `appointed as auditor of a friendly society under section 72 of or Schedule 14 to the Friendly Societies Act 1992`
            THEN `coa26 support either answer` `that friendly society is an insurer` `that friendly society is an issuer whose transferable securities are admitted to trading on a UK regulated market`
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) a person appointed as auditor of a friendly society under section 72 of or Schedule 14 to the Friendly Societies Act 1992, where that society is—"
        `limb (h) prescribed person` MEANS
            CONSIDER `appointed as auditor of a prescribed person under a prescribed enactment authorising or requiring the appointment`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(h) a person appointed as auditor of a prescribed person under a prescribed enactment authorising or requiring the appointment"
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "prescribed" means prescribed by an order of the Secretary of State (s 1210(3)), which is not among the sources

-- src:17014 | and the expressions “statutory audit” and “statutory audit work” are to be construed accordingly.
@ref s 1210(1) the expressions "statutory audit" and "statutory audit work" (src:17014)
GIVEN `the audit is carried out by a person who is a statutory auditor under subsection (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1210(1) the audit is a statutory audit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the audit is carried out by a person who is a statutory auditor under subsection (1)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the text says only that the expressions "are to be construed accordingly", not that an audit by anyone else is not a statutory audit
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the borrowed answer to s 1210(1) is not known

-- src:17014 | and the expressions “statutory audit” and “statutory audit work” are to be construed accordingly.
@ref s 1210(1) the expressions "statutory audit" and "statutory audit work" (src:17014)
GIVEN `the work is work done for the purposes of a statutory audit under subsection (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1210(1) the work is statutory audit work` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the work is work done for the purposes of a statutory audit under subsection (1)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "statutory audit work" is only "to be construed accordingly"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the borrowed answer is not known

-- src:17015 | (2) In this Part “audited person” means the person in respect of whom a statutory audit is conducted.
@ref s 1210(2) "audited person" (src:17015)
GIVEN `an audit is conducted in respect of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that audit is a statutory audit` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1210(2) the person is an audited person` MEANS
    IF `an audit is conducted in respect of the person`
    THEN `that audit is a statutory audit`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“audited person” means the person in respect of whom a statutory audit is conducted"

