-- ---- s 1211: Eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor: overview ------------------------------

-- src:17026 | A person is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor only if the person is so eligible—
-- src:17027 | (a) by virtue of Chapter 2 (individuals and firms), or
-- src:17028 | (b) by virtue of Chapter 3 (Comptroller and Auditor General, etc).
@ref s 1211 Eligibility for appointment as a statutory auditor: overview (src:17026-17028)
GIVEN `the person is eligible by virtue of Chapter 2 (individuals and firms)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is eligible by virtue of Chapter 3 (Comptroller and Auditor General, etc)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1211 the person is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` MEANS
    -- "only if": a necessary condition. JUST FALSE when neither Chapter makes the person eligible; NOTHING otherwise,
    -- because the overview does not itself say the person is eligible (ss 1212 and 1226 say that).
    IF `coa26 support the answer is JUST FALSE` (`coa26 support either answer` `the person is eligible by virtue of Chapter 2 (individuals and firms)` `the person is eligible by virtue of Chapter 3 (Comptroller and Auditor General, etc)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor only if the person is so eligible"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "only if" states a necessary condition; eligibility itself is decided by section 1212 or section 1226
